{"term":"glow","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:a4773891f701a51552","definition":"To emit heat and light without a flame.","example":"Iron glows red hot when heated to near its melting point.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["aglow","glew","GloFish","glower","glowing","glow-in-the-dark","glownigger","glow up","outglow","glowy","reglow"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:77a3d5f12e35fa5a66","definition":"Of a fire: to emit heat and light.","example":"The fire was still glowing after ten hours.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["aglow","glew","GloFish","glower","glowing","glow-in-the-dark","glownigger","glow up","outglow","glowy","reglow"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7be1c6b8e3a738a44e","definition":"To emit light brightly and steadily as if heated to a high temperature; to shine.","example":"[N]ovv glovv'd the Firmament / VVith living Saphirs: […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["aglow","glew","GloFish","glower","glowing","glow-in-the-dark","glownigger","glow up","outglow","glowy","reglow"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:523680dcb60574a022","definition":"To be very hot; also, to be on fire; to burn.","example":"[T]he torrid Zone / Glovvs vvith the paſſing and repaſſing Sun.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["aglow","glew","GloFish","glower","glowing","glow-in-the-dark","glownigger","glow up","outglow","glowy","reglow"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:761e4a114ae40776ab","definition":"Of a colour: to be bright; also, of a thing: to have a bright colour.","example":"The new baby’s room glows with bright, loving colours.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, intransitive","wordFamily":["aglow","glew","GloFish","glower","glowing","glow-in-the-dark","glownigger","glow up","outglow","glowy","reglow"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ee25cda762f41af323","definition":"Of a person: to display intense emotion.","example":"a healthy glow","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, intransitive","wordFamily":["aglow","glew","GloFish","glower","glowing","glow-in-the-dark","glownigger","glow up","outglow","glowy","reglow"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9695c85cc3e22d3181","definition":"Of a person's body or a part of it: to feel hot and often to flush (“become suffused with a reddish colour”) as well, due to an emotional response, exertion, etc.","example":"After their workout, the gymnasts’ faces were glowing.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, intransitive","wordFamily":["aglow","glew","GloFish","glower","glowing","glow-in-the-dark","glownigger","glow up","outglow","glowy","reglow"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1f7aecc579bf9b9260","definition":"To be involved in an (chiefly online) undercover sting operation, especially by American federal agencies.","example":"If this post glows any brighter I'm going to need sunglasses. 😄🕶👌","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Internet, US, figuratively","register":"Internet, US, figuratively, intransitive","wordFamily":["aglow","glew","GloFish","glower","glowing","glow-in-the-dark","glownigger","glow up","outglow","glowy","reglow"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:293c4f80b60b210617","definition":"To create a threatening online post that may involve violence, and look suspicious enough to attract a police investigation.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Internet, US, figuratively","register":"Internet, US, figuratively, intransitive","wordFamily":["aglow","glew","GloFish","glower","glowing","glow-in-the-dark","glownigger","glow up","outglow","glowy","reglow"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5613ab53cd23a119c8","definition":"To emit (flame).","example":"Shall Pagan Pages glovv celeſtial Flame, / And Chriſtian, languiſh?","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic, obsolete","register":"archaic, obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["aglow","glew","GloFish","glower","glowing","glow-in-the-dark","glownigger","glow up","outglow","glowy","reglow"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:91b058fef199d12b03","definition":"To expose (someone) to the authorities.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Internet, figuratively","register":"Internet, figuratively, transitive","wordFamily":["aglow","glew","GloFish","glower","glowing","glow-in-the-dark","glownigger","glow up","outglow","glowy","reglow"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4248425c92edf2f852","definition":"To make (something) hot; to heat.","example":"On each ſide her, / Stood pretty Dimpled Boyes, like ſmiling Cupids, / VVith diuers coulour'd Fannes vvhoſe vvinde did ſeeme / To gloue the delicate cheekes vvhich they did coole, / And vvhat they vndid did.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["aglow","glew","GloFish","glower","glowing","glow-in-the-dark","glownigger","glow up","outglow","glowy","reglow"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7c8e6f3c42d09943df","definition":"A state of heat and light being emitted by a hot object.","example":"The struggling spark of good within, / Just smother'd in the strife of sin, / They quicken to a timely glow, / The pure flame spreading high and low.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["aglow","glew","GloFish","glower","glowing","glow-in-the-dark","glownigger","glow up","outglow","glowy","reglow","afterglow","airglow","Asian glow","aspenglow","candleglow","counterglow","Day-Glo","dayglow","electroglow","evenglow","foreglow","glow-beetle","glowboy","glo